 {"ref":"Fliss, Freivogel & Kontou, The double smeared null energy condition, arXiv:2111.05772","effect":"confirms","what":"Restates F-R exactly ('finite lower bounds of null QEIs do not exist ... vacuum-plus-two-particle states'); proves that smearing in BOTH null directions gives a finite state-independent bound for free scalars in Minkowski (DSNEC, eq.1, 4D eq.136), and reproduces F-R's timelike QNEI (III.10) as its eq.(99). Confirms the tree's 'the DOMAIN of the smearing matters' within free fields.","read_status":"READ (pp.1-5, 8, 11, 15-20, 24, 27, 32-33)"},
 {"ref":"Fliss & Rolph, Curious QNEIs from QNEC, arXiv:2510.26247v2 (Apr 2026)","effect":"narrows","what":"Confirms the finite-segment no-go and gives a general argument beyond free fields (Sec. 3.1: Reeh-Schlieder makes INT g T_vv non-positive-semidefinite; dilatation + boost preserving the null line scale it by lambda^(d-2), so no state-independent bound) -- the argument uses dilatation covariance (CFT). It narrows the reach of a blanket 'no null QEI in d>2': in interacting CFTs with d>2 it derives state-independent QNEIs for null energy on a finite null interval in (u,v), smeared with a modular-kernel M and integrated uniformly over the d-2 transverse directions (eq.1.7/4.2; state-independent only through O(eps_u^0)). 'No QI along a single null geodesic' still stands; 'no QI on any finite null region' does not.","read_status":"READ (pp.1-8, 16-19, 26-28, refs)"},
